# SAIMAIL CURRENT STATE

> **V6-03, the SAIPEN turn-entry hook evaluation, is implemented in the
> development checkout (T-117).** The SAIPEN-owned turn-entry read already
> exists: SAIPEN T-1497 makes `saipen continue`/`status` JSON carry unread
> telegram counts from `saimail-local --json saipen telegrams` when the
> per-machine `SAIMAIL_WORKSPACE` carrier is set. T-117 ran it end to end
> against this checkout and fixed the defect it found on the SAIMAIL side:
> header-only reads (`inbox`, `saipen telegrams|enter|brief`) used to take both
> private keys out of os-store custody on every call. They now use the
> secret-free `load_workspace_headers`: no private key, no credential-store
> read, and a locked store still yields counts. Open, Reopen, send and reply
> keep the full fail-closed load. Checkout-only; frozen `0.0.2a3` does not
> contain it. T-117 lifecycle facts come only from STATE, BOARD and LOG.
> Roadmap v6 §15; decision D-059; contract `spec/26-SAITELEMES-v0.md` §7.

> **T-113 DONE (E-1527): receiver re-read continuity is implemented.**
> V6-02 / READ_REREAD_GAP is resolved by T-113 in the development checkout.
> Open is first-read only (UNREAD to READ); Open still refuses READ. Explicit
> Reopen re-authenticates/decrypts READ within its budget, fails closed and
> leaves durable state and sealed bytes unchanged. Entry, selection and refresh
> remain metadata-only; content appears only after explicit Open or Reopen.
> The checkout is ahead of frozen `0.0.2a3` by checkout-only T-108, T-109,
> T-110, T-113 and T-117 product work, with T-107/T-115 release-evidence repairs.
> Frozen `0.0.2a3` does not contain T-113. T-114 DONE (E-1541) completed the
> capability/recovery truth reconciliation. Active Work, if any, and its
> phase come only from `.saipen/STATE.md`, BOARD and LOG; this document names
> no active owner. The next separate capability direction is evaluation of
> the SAIPEN-owned Work Desk / SAITELEMES turn-entry hook; T-114 did not
> implement it, and starting it requires its own Work, source and admission.
> Do not implement the saved T-113 design again.

> **T-110 DONE (2026-09-23, development checkout):** SAIPEN Work Desk v0 adds
> `saipen enter` and `saipen brief`: local participation/seat checks, current
> work plus all unread topics within one bounded page, and context-checked
> continuation. SAIPEN `init`/`telegram` now require project IDENTITY.
> Guide: `humbox/SAIPEN-WORK-DESK.md`; contract: `spec/27-SAIPEN-WORK-DESK-v0.md`;
