## V6-02 RECEIVER RE-READ CONTINUITY (T-113)

**T-113 DONE; V6-02 DONE via T-113.** The former READ_REREAD_GAP is resolved.
`PostOfficeSession.reopen_message`, `workspace.reopen_message`, the distinct
`saimail-local reopen` command and GUI `Reopen` are implemented. Open remains
UNREAD-only; Reopen requires READ, re-verifies sender/recipient, receipt/index
and sealed bytes under the lifecycle lock, consumes its open budget and
preserves READ without plaintext persistence. Expiry/tombstone and crash
ambiguity still refuse. Selecting, refreshing or restarting never decrypts.

Evidence: `tests/test_reread_continuation.py` (25 T-113 controls), stable API
`lab/stable_local_api.json`, spec/03 and spec/25 §4.3. Historical T-113 full
suite: 2549 passed / 0 failed / 0 errors / 0 skipped (E-1521); independent
review PASS E-1524; closure E-1527. T-115 repaired D3 evidence monotonicity
(44 focused / 2522 full at that checkpoint, E-1514); T-115 DONE E-1518.
These checkout-only results are not evidence that frozen a3 contains Reopen.

## V6-03 SAIPEN TURN-ENTRY HOOK EVALUATION (T-117)

**V6-03 implemented in the checkout by T-117** (source SRC-106, "continue by
meaning; humbox is the beacon"). T-117 lifecycle facts (phase, closure event)
live only in STATE, BOARD and LOG.

- **Found:** the SAIPEN side was already built. SAIPEN T-1497 (its SRC-113)
  added `tools/saipen_engine/telegrams.py`: at `continue`/`status` it runs
  `saimail-local --json saipen telegrams --workspace $SAIMAIL_WORKSPACE
  --scan-budget 200` and reports `unread`, `on_current_work` and `complete`,
  counts only. A live run against this checkout (two scratch mailboxes, topics
  `T-117` and `T-7`) gave `unread 2, on_current_work 1, complete true`.
- **Defect (SAIMAIL side):** the read called the full `load_workspace`. In
  os-store custody that retrieves both private keys from the OS credential store
  on every automatic turn entry, only to count headers, and a locked or
  prompting store turned the count into `CUSTODY_ACCESS_FAILED` (SAIPEN
  `ERROR`). Probe: 2 secret reads per call; locked store refused.
- **Fix:** `workspace.load_workspace_headers` returns `WorkspaceHeaders`, a
  public-key-only view. It runs every public check of the full load (marker
  fingerprints, identity field set and marker agreement, os-store public
  projection and handles), builds no private key and never reads the store.
  `inbox`, `saipen telegrams`, `saipen enter` and `saipen brief` use it; open,
  reopen, send, reply and `saipen telegram` keep the full fail-closed load.
  Probe after: 0 secret reads; locked store: counts returned, `open` still
  refused with `CUSTODY_ACCESS_FAILED`.
- **Boundary stated:** a raw identity whose private key no longer matches the
  marker still lists headers; every key-using load refuses it. The header view
  proves the public identity, not possession of the private one.
- **Evidence:** `tests/test_turn_entry_headers.py` (8 controls, including the
  pinned SAIPEN-consumed fields `ok`, `match_count`, `exhausted`,
  `items[].topic`, exit code, refusal code in `status`); red controls on the
  exact pre-T-117 bytes (7 of 8 fail) and on a weakened marker-only loader
  (both parity controls fail): `.saipen/evidence/T-117-turn-entry/`.
- **Cross-project findings for the SAIPEN protocolist (not changed here):**
  SAIPEN reads a refusal code from `code`, but `LOCAL_WORKSPACE_COMMAND_1`
  carries it in `status`, so its `ERROR` detail never names the cause; its
  `read_command` hint interpolates paths unquoted; and it counts whatever
  mailbox the carrier names without comparing `workspace.seat` with the acting
  seat. Filed as `%LOCALAPPDATA%\saipen\protocol_incidents\inbox\SAI-DEFECT-20260924-turn-entry-telegrams-refusal-code-and-read-command.md` with body
  `.saipen/evidence/T-117-turn-entry/SAIPEN-FINDINGS.md`.
- **Release truth:** checkout-only, not inside frozen `0.0.2a3`; no version
  bump, rebuild, tag, push or publication.

